{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall look at the affliction.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: the priest does not examine the affliction on the first day, for he must isolate him for seven days, and it is written ״וראה הכהן אותו ביום השביעי״, and it is impossible to examine it on the Sabbath. And not on the second day either, for if he needs to isolate him for two weeks, the seventh day of the second week's isolation would fall on the Sabbath, which is the thirteenth day; therefore they said 'two weeks,' meaning thirteen days." "<b>and the hair in the affliction has turned white, and the appearance of the affliction is deeper than the skin of his flesh.</b> Rashi of blessed memory explained: every white appearance is 'deep,' like the appearance of the sun being deeper than the shadow." "<b>And he wrote.</b> The Ramban of blessed memory wrote in his commentary on this: there is a whiteness that gives off a brilliance and a glint to the eyes like the appearance of the sun, and the eye cannot receive that hue of whiteness, and therefore it appears to it as deep — for the appearance of the sun, which is deeper than the shadow, is because the eye receives the hue of blackness and it is fixed in it and bears it; but the hue of whiteness, the eye does not receive it, and it scatters the power of sight and pushes it away, and therefore it appears deep. And behold, the whiteness of the bright spot (בהרת), which is bright and fierce as snow — sight is weakened by it just as it is weakened by the place of the sun, provided there is no black hair in it, for then the power of sight takes hold of the blackness, and from there it extends throughout the entire area of the affliction and does not flee from it. But the white boil (שאת) is white, yet the whiteness is not brilliant and does not weaken sight; rather sight takes hold of it and draws near to it, and it appears to it as close and elevated — like the appearance of the stars, which appear as though they are high in the firmament."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:12.059461981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}